# Normalize line endings: store everything as LF in the repo, regardless
# of what line ending a given OS/editor/script writes to the working tree.
# This is what stops `git status` from showing false "modified" diffs when
# a file is regenerated on Windows (CRLF) but was committed as LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Transfer Lab release files are published as reviewed artifacts and are
# checksummed by SHA256SUMS.txt in the same folder. Store every byte exactly
# as shipped -- no line-ending normalization -- or the recorded checksums stop
# matching the committed content on a fresh clone.
docs/prototypes/transfer-lab-v2.2.1/** -text -eol
